<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 5 July, from 1687 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-newton" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isaac-newton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1687 CE <span class="tih-ago">339 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Isaac Newton publishes the Principia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Newton's Philosophiae Naturalis <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/principia-mathematica-newton">Principia</a> Mathematica was published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. It set out the laws of motion and universal gravitation, giving physics the framework that dominated science for more than two centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1830 CE <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French forces capture Algiers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> surrendered to a French expeditionary force, beginning 132 years of French rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. The colonisation ended only after a long and bloody war of independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 CE <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Booth begins the mission that becomes the Salvation Army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Methodist preacher William Booth began evangelising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>'s East End, founding the Christian Mission. Renamed the Salvation Army in 1878, it grew into a worldwide church and charity.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 CE <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis Réard unveils the bikini at a Paris swimming pool</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Engineer and designer Louis Réard presented his two-piece swimsuit at the Piscine Molitor, modelled by dancer Micheline Bernardini. He named it after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bikini-atoll">Bikini Atoll</a>, where atomic tests had just begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1948 CE <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The National Health Service launches in Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aneurin Bevan's National Health Service began, offering comprehensive care free at the point of use to everyone in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. It became one of the defining institutions of the post-war welfare state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1962 CE <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Algeria becomes independent from France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> proclaimed independence, 132 years to the day after French troops took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. It followed an eight-year war of liberation and a referendum in which Algerians voted overwhelmingly for independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a></div></div></li></ol>
